msgid "A series of links that provide context to this bundle."
msgstr ""

# null
#: Bundle.link@comment
msgid "Both Bundle.link and Bundle.entry.link are defined to support providing additional context when Bundles are used (e.g. [HATEOAS](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HATEOAS)). \n\nBundle.entry.link corresponds to links found in the HTTP header if the resource in the entry was [read](http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/http.html#read) directly.\n\nThis specification defines some specific uses of Bundle.link for [searching](http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/search.html#conformance) and [paging](http://hl7.org/fhir/R4/http.html#paging), but no specific uses for Bundle.entry.link, and no defined function in a transaction - the meaning is implementation specific."
msgstr ""

